// g7250_control_i2c_mock.repl — minimal ACKing I2C slaves for the Control boot.
//
// Overlay for g7250_control.repl (load AFTER it). Same rationale as the Main
// overlay: Renode's STM32F7_I2C only drives the HAL TXIS/TC/STOPF flags when a
// slave is present, so without these the Control's I2C bring-up would crawl on
// per-byte 100 ms timeouts. Addresses from control_unit/docs/peripherals.md:
//   I2C1: GT911 capacitive touch 0x14 (reset selects 0x14; fallback 0x5D)
//   I2C2: AIC3204 codec 0x18, PCA9557 I/O expander 0x19
// Mock bytes suffice to reach the GUI service loop; swap one for a functional
// slave (models/devices/control_i2c.py) when a test needs real device data.

i2c1_gt911:     Mocks.DummyI2CSlave @ i2c1 0x14
i2c1_gt911_alt: Mocks.DummyI2CSlave @ i2c1 0x5D
i2c2_aic3204:   Mocks.DummyI2CSlave @ i2c2 0x18
i2c2_pca9557:   Mocks.DummyI2CSlave @ i2c2 0x19
